  "id": "frontal-association-area",
  "term": "frontal association area",
  "definition": "The frontal association area is a frontal brain region described as a higher-level control center for forming and regulating behavior. It is closely linked to higher cognitive functions such as executive control, working memory, logical reasoning, fluid intelligence, and other advanced thinking and self-directed action skills.",
